#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:4
msgid "s390 Secure IPL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:6
msgid ""
"Secure IPL, also known as secure boot, enables s390-ccw virtual machines to "
"verify the integrity of guest kernels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:9
msgid ""
"For technical details of this feature, see the :doc:`specs document </specs/"
"s390x-secure-ipl>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:12
msgid ""
"This document explains how to use secure IPL with s390x in QEMU. It covers "
"the command line options for providing certificates and enabling secure IPL, "
"the different IPL modes (Normal, Audit, and Secure), and system requirements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:16
msgid ""
"A quickstart guide is provided to demonstrate how to generate certificates, "
"sign images, and start a guest in Secure Mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:21
msgid "Secure IPL Command Line Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:23
msgid ""
"The s390-ccw-virtio machine type supports secure IPL. These parameters allow "
"users to provide certificates and enable secure IPL directly via the command "
"line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:28
msgid "Providing Certificates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:30
msgid ""
"The certificate store can be populated by supplying a list of X.509 "
"certificate file paths or directories containing certificate files on the "
"command-line:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:33
msgid "Note: certificate files must have a .pem extension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:35
#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:83
msgid ""
"qemu-system-s390x -machine s390-ccw-virtio,boot-certs.0.path=/.../qemu/certs,"
"boot-certs.1.path=/another/path/cert.pem ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:40
msgid "Enabling Secure IPL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:42
msgid ""
"Secure IPL is enabled by explicitly setting ``secure-boot=on``; if not "
"specified, secure boot is considered off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:45
msgid "qemu-system-s390x -machine s390-ccw-virtio,secure-boot=on|off"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:51
msgid "IPL Modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:53
msgid ""
"Multiple IPL modes are available to differentiate between the various IPL "
"configurations. These modes are mutually exclusive and enabled based on "
"specific combinations of the ``secure-boot`` and ``boot-certs`` options on "
"the QEMU command line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:59
msgid "Normal Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:61
msgid ""
"The absence of both certificates and the ``secure-boot`` option will attempt "
"to IPL a guest without secure IPL operations. No checks are performed, and "
"no warnings/errors are reported.  This is the default mode, and can be "
"explicitly enabled with ``secure-boot=off``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:66
#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:81
#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:94
msgid "Configuration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:68
msgid "qemu-system-s390x -machine s390-ccw-virtio ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:73
msgid "Audit Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:75
msgid ""
"When the certificate store is populated with at least one certificate and no "
"additional secure IPL parameters are provided on the command line, then "
"secure IPL will proceed in \"audit mode\". All secure IPL operations will be "
"performed with signature verification errors reported as non-disruptive "
"warnings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:88
msgid "Secure Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:90
msgid ""
"When the ``secure-boot=on`` option is set and certificates are provided, a "
"secure boot is performed with error reporting enabled. The boot process "
"aborts if any error occurs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:96
msgid ""
"qemu-system-s390x -machine s390-ccw-virtio,secure-boot=on,boot-certs.0."
"path=/.../qemu/certs,boot-certs.1.path=/another/path/cert.pem ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:102
msgid "Constraints"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:104
msgid ""
"The following constraints apply when attempting to boot an s390x guest in "
"secure mode:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:107
msgid "z16 or \"qemu\" CPU model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:108
msgid "certificates must be in X.509 PEM format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:109
msgid "only support for SCSI scheme of virtio-blk/virtio-scsi devices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:110
msgid "a boot device must be specified"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:111
msgid ""
"any unsupported devices (e.g., ECKD and VFIO) or non-eligible devices (e.g., "
"network) will cause the entire boot process to terminate early, with an "
"error logged to the console."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:117
msgid "Secure IPL Quickstart"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:120
msgid "Build QEMU with gnutls enabled"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:122
msgid "./configure … --enable-gnutls"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:127
msgid "Generate certificate (e.g. via certtool)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:129
msgid ""
"A private key is required before generating a certificate. This key must be "
"kept secure and confidential."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:132
msgid "Use an RSA private key for signing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:134
msgid "certtool --generate-privkey > key.pem"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:138
msgid ""
"A self-signed certificate requires the organization name. Use the ``cert."
"info`` template to pre-fill values and avoid interactive prompts from "
"certtool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:141
msgid ""
"cat > cert.info <<EOF\n"
"cn = \"My Name\"\n"
"expiration_days = 365\n"
"cert_signing_key\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"certtool --generate-self-signed \\\n"
"         --load-privkey key.pem \\\n"
"         --template cert.info \\\n"
"         --hash=SHA256 \\\n"
"         --outfile cert.pem"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:156
msgid "Sign Images (e.g. via sign-file)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:158
msgid "signing must be performed on a guest filesystem"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:159
msgid ""
"sign-file script used in the example below is located within the kernel "
"source repo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:162
msgid ""
"./sign-file sha256 key.pem cert.pem /boot/vmlinuz-…\n"
"./sign-file sha256 key.pem cert.pem /usr/lib/s390-tools/stage3.bin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:167
msgid ""
"Note: re-signing a component will not verify correctly; the existing "
"signature must be stripped before a new one is applied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:171
msgid "Run zipl with secure boot enabled"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:173
msgid "zipl must be performed on a guest filesystem"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:175
msgid "zipl --secure 1 -V"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:180
msgid "Command line options for starting the guest"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/s390x/secure-ipl.rst:182
msgid ""
"qemu-system-s390x -machine s390-ccw-virtio,secure-boot=on,boot-certs.0."
"path=cert.pem ..."
msgstr ""
